                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0ea09ce5-e0c2-36f5-b9f8-a52a4bf6bc0b",
                        "entry_id": "ecb136b3-2eb2-340f-810f-e1c53448c0d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "минерал, прозрачная ювелирная разновидность оливина"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f4a6b3a-bb40-4292-9988-6a38f6d60ea0",
                                "sense_id": "0ea09ce5-e0c2-36f5-b9f8-a52a4bf6bc0b",
                                "text": "В результате получались играющие разными цветами драгоценные и полудрагоценные камни: изумруды, хризолиты, аквамарины, тяжеловесы (благородный топаз), аметисты, а больше всего — раух-топазы (дымчатого цвета горный хрусталь) и просто горный бесцве́тный хрусталь."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "685c3377-42bd-467e-b038-e04c2e4539aa",
                        "source_entry_id": "ecb136b3-2eb2-340f-810f-e1c53448c0d9",
                        "source_sense_id": "0ea09ce5-e0c2-36f5-b9f8-a52a4bf6bc0b",
                        "target_lang_word": "peridot",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "peridot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d222c351-d00d-33cc-a24e-2fed467c8254",
                                        "entry_id": "19ca767c-1e2e-3366-96aa-276c89cd8a6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A transparent olive green form of olivine, used as a gem."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "902c6bd3-05de-4e30-9e3a-05bfa265b2ca",
                                                "sense_id": "d222c351-d00d-33cc-a24e-2fed467c8254",
                                                "text": "Gem-quality olivine is known as peridot, which has a subtle green light all its own."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76df1723-d7e5-4ff2-b35c-8b1ce3aa6e2d",
                                                "sense_id": "d222c351-d00d-33cc-a24e-2fed467c8254",
                                                "text": "Although there are dozens of different types of gems, among the best known and most important are […]. (Common gem materials not addressed in this article include amber, amethyst, chalcedony, garnet, lazurite, malachite, opals, peridot, rhodonite, spinel, tourmaline, turquoise and zircon.)"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f8d6824b-695f-3099-9c95-540b1fed0603",
                                        "entry_id": "19ca767c-1e2e-3366-96aa-276c89cd8a6c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A yellow-green color, like that of the peridot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "019cd0c7-49c4-49a9-b44b-4ac0477430d2",
                        "source_entry_id": "ecb136b3-2eb2-340f-810f-e1c53448c0d9",
                        "source_sense_id": "0ea09ce5-e0c2-36f5-b9f8-a52a4bf6bc0b",
                        "target_lang_word": "chrysolite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "chrysolite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                        "entry_id": "d99aee02-9cfa-301b-b065-ef95911e13d7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Originally, any of various green-coloured gems; later specifically peridot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c142a448-5829-4509-99eb-2c3c243f0169",
                                                "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                                "text": "Fran. Rueus[…]say as much of the chrysolite, a friend of wisdome, an enemy to folly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e7bd390-16f8-49aa-ade5-59d103080ca3",
                                                "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                                "text": "And before he died, Taran-Ish had scrawled upon the altar of chrysolite with coarse shaky strokes the sign of DOOM."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa90ed35-d609-4bd4-9795-613435e82bfa",
                                                "sense_id": "5942032f-0d09-3f96-920b-c619e15c7e0c",
                                                "text": "A piece of marigold or bay leaf was imbedded in the metal, and over it a carbuncle or chrysolite was placed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
